1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,361
Been through two or three anti-dandruff shampoos and the flakes still keep coming back?

2
00:00:04,681 --> 00:00:09,659
The bottle in your shower might not be the problem - your plate could be working against it.

3
00:00:09,979 --> 00:00:18,940
A yeast called Malassezia lives on your scalp's oil, and breaking it down releases oleic acid that irritates skin in people sensitive to it.

4
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:22,555
Three foods in the American diet can each fuel that cycle.

5
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:32,551
First, sweets like donuts and cookies spike blood sugar fast, raising insulin and IGF-1, which tells oil glands to make more sebum for the yeast.

6
00:00:32,871 --> 00:00:35,241
Second, dairy like whole milk and ice cream.

7
00:00:35,561 --> 00:00:43,737
One clinical study found dairy among the foods most linked to flare-ups, and researchers point to hormones in milk that push oil glands into overdrive.

8
00:00:44,057 --> 00:00:47,381
Third, fried food like French fries and fried chicken.

9
00:00:47,701 --> 00:00:53,984
Frying oils are heavy in omega-6 fats, which may drive inflammation and shift your sebum's makeup.

10
00:00:54,304 --> 00:01:02,816
Try berries or nuts instead of donuts and cookies, unsweetened soy milk instead of whole milk, and oven-roasted or grilled versions instead of fried.

11
00:01:03,136 --> 00:01:05,632
Salmon and other fatty fish can help too.
